<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Dalamud.NET.Sdk/15.0.0">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>0.1.0.0</Version>
    <Author>Raiden Shinryu</Author>
    <!-- The player sees "Gleam"; the assembly, namespaces and config file keep the original TidyUp name so existing settings carry over. -->
    <Name>Gleam</Name>
    <Punchline>Cleans and organizes your inventory. Nothing happens until you press the button.</Punchline>
    <Description>Gleam cleans and organizes your inventory.

Clean: it finds junk in your bags, armoury chest, saddlebag, retainers and glamour dresser and shows it in one list. You choose whether to sell on the market board, sell to vendors or discard, then press one button.

Organize: layouts move the items you keep to where you want them. For example, materia to the saddlebag, spare gear to a retainer and gear-set pieces to the armoury chest.

Nothing is changed until you press the button. Items that will be cleaned or moved are highlighted in the game's bag windows.

Commands: /gleam or /gl. Sub-commands: organize, history, settings, stop.

Other plugins:
- None are needed for cleaning and organizing. You open the saddlebag and your retainers yourself; Gleam does the rest.
- vnavmesh and Lifestream: needed only for hands-free mode, where Gleam travels to the inn and the bell for you.
- AutoRetainer: optional. Lets Gleam discard junk after each retainer's ventures.
- Allagan Tools: optional. Shows retainer contents without summoning them.
Market prices come from Universalis and need an internet connection.</Description>
    <RepoUrl>https://github.com/savvasleousis/TidyUp</RepoUrl>
    <Tags>inventory;cleanup;discard;organize;sort;retainer;saddlebag;market board;glamour;qol</Tags>
    <RootNamespace>TidyUp</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TidyUp</AssemblyName>
    <LangVersion>14.0</LangVersion>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\TidyUp.Core\TidyUp.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="Data\curated.json">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Visible>true</Visible>
    </Content>
    <Content Include="images\*.png">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Visible>true</Visible>
    </Content>
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
